    IDS_RULE_HELP                  "Rule syntax:   allow|block  [in|out|both]  [ip4|ip6]  [tcp|udp|icmp|proto N]\n               [from|to|remote|local ADDR]  [sport|dport|rport|lport|port P]  [type N]  [app NAME|PATH]\n\n  ADDR  1.2.3.4   1.2.3.0/24   10.0.0.1-10.0.0.50   2001:db8::/32   (a bare ADDR = remote)\n  P     443   27015-27030\n  NAME  discord.exe  or  discord     PATH  C:\\Tools\\nc.exe   (a value with spaces goes in ""quotes"")\n  remote/local and rport/lport follow the packet direction (outbound: remote = destination).\n  ""port"" matches either side. Rules are checked top-down, the first match wins; packets that\n  match no rule follow the default policy.\n\nExamples:\n  block out tcp dport 443              no outgoing HTTPS\n  block udp rport 27015-27030          cut a game server range, both ways\n  allow remote 192.168.0.0/16          keep the LAN reachable\n  block in icmp type 8                 ignore incoming ping\n  block 203.0.113.7                    one host, any protocol\n  block app discord.exe                one program (its TCP and UDP sockets)\n  block app ""C:\\Tools\\net cat.exe""    one copy of a program, by its path\n  allow out udp dport 53               DNS (put it above a broader block)\n"
